{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the morning sun surprisingly bright. He stretched, a familiar ache in his back, but something felt…off. The colors were too vibrant, the light too perfect. He glanced at his hands, flexing his fingers. They felt…real, yet somehow pixelated. A strange, echoing sound resonated around him, like a poorly rendered sound effect. He looked out the window, and the world outside wasn't his suburban street. It was a meticulously crafted, almost hyper-realistic recreation of a medieval village, complete with cobblestone streets and thatched-roof houses. A digital rooster crowed, and a nearby blacksmith hammered away, the clang of metal echoing with unnerving precision. Panic began to bubble in Arthur's chest as he realized, with chilling certainty, that he wasn't in his own life anymore. He was inside a video game.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of bed, his legs feeling oddly stiff. The room was identical to his own, but the furniture seemed…too pristine. He touched the bedside table, and it felt solid, but with a slight, almost imperceptible shimmer. A notification popped up in his vision – a subtle overlay he hadn't noticed before. It read: \"Player Arthur - Level 1. Quest: Find the missing scroll of Eldoria.\" He stared at the message, his mind reeling. This was insane. He was a character in a game, a simple adventurer with no skills or experience. He needed to figure out how to get out, or at least survive long enough to understand the rules of this bizarre new reality. The world around him waited, a vast, digital landscape brimming with possibilities – and dangers.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7354406118392944}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -1.5083379745483398}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -6.9141146923357155e-06}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.15686462819576263}, {"token": "▁morning", "logprob": -0.16190676391124725},